 "findings": [
  {
   "severity": "medium",
   "title": "Each background/foreground cycle starts another game loop (leak)",
   "detail": "The visibilitychange handler (index.html:1044-1047) sets running=false when hidden and calls requestAnimationFrame(frame) again when visible. Browsers keep the rAF callback that was already queued and run it after the page comes back, and frame() reschedules itself once running is true again. So every background/foreground cycle adds one more self-perpetuating loop. Measured callbacks per displayed frame after 0..5 cycles: 1,2,3,4,5,6. The extra loops get dt~0 but each one calls update() and draw() again, so CPU and battery cost grow with every app switch, which mobile users do constantly. The clumsy session already ran 2 loops.",
   "repro": "Open game; background and foreground the tab 5 times; count frame() invocations per rAF timestamp (probes.backgroundCycles in results.json).",
   "fix": "Keep the rAF id and cancelAnimationFrame(id) on hidden, or start a new loop on visible only if none is pending (e.g. a `loopScheduled` flag set in frame())."
  },
  {
   "severity": "medium",
   "title": "Tapping a grown tree spawns unlimited apples (no cap, trim() not applied)",
   "detail": "The canvas pointerdown handler (index.html:1009) runs make(\"apple\") on every tap of a grown tree and never calls trim(). 300 rapid taps raised the entity count from 7 to 307 apples. Frame script time went from ~1.3 ms to 4.9 ms and keeps growing. Apples only go away when a rabbit or bear eats them, so a child tapping the tree builds an ever-heavier scene.",
   "repro": "Fresh world, tap the starting tree rapidly 300 times; __ww.state().n = 307 (probes.treeTapFlood).",
   "fix": "Cap apples per tree (e.g. max 5 live apples) or call trim() after spawning; optionally rate-limit tree taps."
  },
  {
   "severity": "low",
   "title": "Parser misses a standalone English word after the same word appears inside another word",
   "detail": "In parse() (index.html:198) the whole-word check does `break` on the first embedded match, so later standalone occurrences are never examined: \"scat cat\" and \"bobcat cat\" both return [], and \"catdog\" returns []. Full-width input common on phone keyboards (ＣＡＴ) is also not recognised.",
   "repro": "__ww.parse(\"scat cat\") -> []; __ww.parse(\"ＣＡＴ\") -> [] (probes.parse).",
   "fix": "Continue searching from idx+1 instead of break (e.g. use a regex with word boundaries), and normalise with s.normalize(\"NFKC\") before matching."
  },
  {
   "severity": "low",
   "title": "Single-character Chinese aliases cause surprising matches",
   "detail": "Aliases 家/心/夜/月 match inside everyday words: 大家好 and 我家 give a house; 開心, 點心 and 心情 give a heart; 夜市 and 月餅 give the moon (and turn day into night). Probably harmless for a toy, but 大家好 creating a house is odd.",
   "repro": "probes.parse in results.json",
   "fix": "Drop the 1-char aliases that are common morphemes, or require them to stand alone."
  },
  {
   "severity": "low",
   "title": "Emoji / invisible input edge cases",
   "detail": "maxlength=16 counts UTF-16 units, so pasted ZWJ emoji are cut mid-sequence in the field. addBlob() (index.html:337) slices 6 code points, which leaves \"👨‍👩‍👧‍\" with a dangling ZWJ, so the blob label renders as a broken family emoji. A zero-width space (\\u200b) passes the empty check (index.html:977, trim() keeps it) and creates an invisible blob labelled \"\".",
   "repro": "Type 👨‍👩‍👧‍👦👨‍👩‍👧‍👦 and submit; type \\u200b and submit.",
   "fix": "Slice by grapheme (Intl.Segmenter) and strip \\p{Cf}/whitespace before the empty check."
  },
  {
   "severity": "low",
   "title": "Live entity count can exceed the 45 cap",
   "detail": "trim() runs only from addWord/addBlob and removes one entity per call. Rain-spawned flowers, sprouting seeds, stars from 星空 and tree apples bypass it: casual peaked at 58 entities and the tree probe reached 307.",
   "repro": "maxEntities in results.json tiers",
   "fix": "Call trim() in a loop until <=45, and also from make()."
  },
  {
   "severity": "low",
   "title": "No crashes; rotation keeps entities in bounds",
   "detail": "Odd inputs caused no page or console errors in any tier: empty, emoji, 60 x \"a\", <b> tags, mixed 中英, ZWSP. All text goes through textContent and canvas fillText, so markup is not injected. Rotating to 844x390 and back kept every entity inside the world and fish inside the pond.",
   "repro": "probes.rotate, tiers.clumsy.runs[0].odd"
  }
 ],
